BT /F2 24 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 790.00 Tm (Marine Plastic Tracker: Model, Data, and Training Explainer) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 743.92 Tm (Prepared from the current codebase on Thursday, July 30, 2026.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 719.30 Tm (This note is written in simple words so we can explain the project clearly to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 703.68 Tm (the panel.) Tj ET
BT /F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 673.06 Tm (1. What the project does) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 639.50 Tm (Our project takes free Sentinel-2 satellite images of the sea, finds pixels that) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 623.88 Tm (may contain floating material, uses AI to decide whether that material is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 608.26 Tm (plastic or not, groups nearby plastic pixels into hotspots, and predicts where) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 592.64 Tm (those hotspots may drift over the next 72 hours.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 568.02 Tm (Simple one-line answer:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 543.40 Tm ("We built a system that looks at satellite images, finds possible floating) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 527.78 Tm (waste, checks whether it is plastic, and shows where it may move next.") Tj ET
BT /F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 497.16 Tm (2. Which model is used?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 463.60 Tm (The main deployed model is `marinenet.onnx`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 438.98 Tm (It is a per-pixel neural network model. In simple words, it looks at one) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 423.36 Tm (candidate pixel at a time and classifies it into one of 4 classes:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 398.74 Tm (- Plastic) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 382.12 Tm (- Algae) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 365.50 Tm (- Sea_Foam) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 348.88 Tm (- Water) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 326.26 Tm (The current shipped model is a 3-seed ensemble of per-pixel MLPs. That means we) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 310.64 Tm (trained the same kind of network multiple times and combined their outputs to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 295.02 Tm (make the result more stable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 270.40 Tm (There is also a second model called Clay. Clay is not the main detector. It is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 254.78 Tm (used as a second opinion verifier for hotspots after the main model has already) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 239.16 Tm (detected possible plastic.) Tj ET
BT /F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 208.54 Tm (3. What is the model trained on?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 174.98 Tm (The final deployed main model is trained on 2 real public benchmark datasets:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 150.36 Tm (- MARIDA) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 133.74 Tm (- MADOS) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 111.12 Tm (These are real Sentinel-2 marine remote-sensing datasets with scientist-provided) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 95.50 Tm (labels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 28 Tm (Marine Plastic Tracker panel explainer) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 505 28 Tm (Page 1) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
