BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 790.00 Tm ("Our project uses a main AI model called `marinenet.onnx`. It is a per-pixel) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 774.38 Tm (neural network that classifies candidate satellite pixels into Plastic, Algae,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 758.76 Tm (Sea_Foam, or Water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 734.14 Tm (We trained the final model on two real labeled benchmark datasets: MARIDA and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 718.52 Tm (MADOS. Together they gave us 1,081,615 labeled training pixels. We stored the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 702.90 Tm (raw datasets in the project's data folder, wrote our own Python loaders, cleaned) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 687.28 Tm (the data, mapped the original labels into our 4 project classes, calculated the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 671.66 Tm (spectral features, and saved clean cache files for training.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 647.04 Tm (Then we trained the model on GPU, tested it on held-out data it had never seen) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 631.42 Tm (before, and exported it to ONNX for live use in the project. The current shipped) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 50 615.80 Tm (model got 98.99% accuracy and 0.8175 Macro-F1 on the combined held-out test.) Tj ET
